WEBVTT

00:33:59.583 --> 00:34:02.184
EP: It's just that I had people
come to my office

00:34:02.208 --> 00:34:04.268
rather than me go to their office.

00:34:04.292 --> 00:34:07.143
AG: Well, the worst case is
when the person is sleeping fine

00:34:07.167 --> 00:34:09.393
because they know
you're fretting, which is --

00:34:09.417 --> 00:34:10.684
EP: That's sadistic.

00:34:10.708 --> 00:34:11.976
AG: Yes.

00:34:12.000 --> 00:34:15.643
But one of the things I'm thinking about
as I sit with this thought is,

00:34:15.667 --> 00:34:19.393
since I first started studying
psychology in college,

00:34:19.417 --> 00:34:21.143
whenever I take values assessments,

00:34:21.167 --> 00:34:23.684
I come out with
two core values at the top,

00:34:23.708 --> 00:34:27.268
one is helping other people
and the other is achieving excellence.

00:34:27.292 --> 00:34:31.893
And I was surprised at first
that relationships came lower